                  "url": "https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"
                }
              ],
              "steps": [
                {
                  "action": "Replace shell=True and shell-specific helpers with subprocess.run using an argument list, shell=False, a fixed executable path and an explicit timeout. Replace pipelines with separate bounded calls or native library operations.",
                  "title": "Use a fixed process invocation",
                  "verification": "Submit spaces, quotes and shell metacharacters as data to a harmless test executable; assert the expected argument vector and that no additional process starts."
                },
                {
                  "action": "Allowlist flags and resource identifiers, reject caller-selected executables, and use an end-of-options delimiter only where the chosen utility supports it. Do not treat shlex.split or shell quoting as authorization.",
                  "title": "Validate argument meaning",
                  "verification": "Test leading-dash filenames, unexpected flags and an interpreter executable; verify policy blocks them before process creation."
                },
                {
                  "action": "Set a permitted working directory and minimal environment, bound output and runtime, and apply a separate low-privilege execution identity where required. Review Windows batch-file behavior on the actual platform.",
                  "title": "Constrain process authority",
                  "verification": "Run denial tests for forbidden files, inherited credentials and excessive output on each deployed operating system."
                }
              ],
              "summary": "Remove shell parsing and constrain the actual executable and its arguments."
            },
            "confidence": "medium",
            "severity": "high",
            "status": "open"
          },
