          "message": {
            "text": "Pickle-compatible deserialization can execute code. This finding identifies a dangerous trust boundary, not proof that the serialized input is attacker controlled. Remediation: Use a nonexecutable serialization format with schema validation. If compatibility requires pickle, accept only authenticated artifacts from a strictly controlled producer. Agent/MCP relevance: A cached agent state, plugin artifact or MCP-uploaded file may reach pickle-compatible loading. Deserialization can execute producer-selected code before downstream data validation. Fix steps: 1. Replace pickle, dill, joblib or equivalent object loading with JSON or another nonexecutable format plus a versioned schema. Reconstruct only explicitly supported application types. Verify: Roundtrip required benign state and reject unexpected type markers, fields and oversized collections without importing producer-selected code. 2. If compatibility requires executable deserialization, authenticate the exact bytes against a producer/key or registry digest established independently of the artifact location. Restrict cache and artifact writers. Verify: Alter one byte and change the producer identity in test artifacts; verify rejection before the deserializer is called. 3. Convert legacy artifacts in a disposable credential-free worker with resource and network limits, then export validated data to the main service. Verify: Verify conversion cannot read main-service secrets or contact forbidden destinations and that failed conversions publish no partial trusted state."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "agentMcpScan/v1": "d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc"
          },
          "properties": {
            "agentMcpRemediation": {
              "agent_mcp_relevance": "A cached agent state, plugin artifact or MCP-uploaded file may reach pickle-compatible loading. Deserialization can execute producer-selected code before downstream data validation.",
              "applicability": [
                "Identify the producer and every write path to the artifact, including shared caches, object stores and task workspaces.",
                "The finding identifies a dangerous loader; it does not show that its input is attacker controlled."
              ],
              "catalog_sha256": "6ea5b70b817f35b68352ce9b7b443b1c01139ba7b94ee2631f5db5ef7521b96e",
