          "message": {
            "text": "A credential-named field contains a nonplaceholder literal. It may be a real secret or test data; validate it without disclosing the value. Remediation: If real, revoke and rotate the credential, remove it from source and history, and load it from a secret manager or environment variable with least privilege. Agent/MCP relevance: A hardcoded model, gateway or downstream-tool key can grant access outside the intended agent session and tenant. Repository or image readers may obtain the credential independently of the agent approval path. Fix steps: 1. Identify the credential owner and permissions using secret-safe metadata. Revoke or rotate real exposed credentials with a staged application update and review provider audit records. Verify: Verify the old credential is rejected and the replacement has only required model/tool scopes; retain redacted rotation evidence. 2. Replace the literal with a secret-manager lookup or runtime injection. Remove it from tracked files, distributed image layers and relevant build artifacts; coordinate any history rewrite with repository owners. Verify: Rescan the source and every retained image layer, and check logs/build artifacts for the old credential through a protected secret-scanning workflow. 3. Use separate per-service or per-tenant credentials where supported and restrict which tool workers receive them. Exclude local secret files from version control and build contexts. Verify: Run a tool that does not need the credential and verify it cannot read it; confirm clean builds do not embed injected build secrets."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "agentMcpScan/v1": "afb2bdb94696690028650faf"
          },
