                  "uri": "mcp.json"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 4,
                  "startLine": 4
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "An MCP launch configuration uses npx, uvx, or a similar ephemeral package runner without an exact package version. The executable artifact can change between launches. Remediation: Pin an exact audited package version and lock or verify transitive artifacts. Prefer preinstalled verified tools in a controlled environment. Agent/MCP relevance: An MCP client often launches a package with its local user permissions and injected credentials. Unpinned npx/uvx resolution can replace the tool implementation between launches without a reviewed configuration change. Fix steps: 1. For npm execution specify an exact package version, including scope where applicable; for uvx use an exact package version or explicit --from package==version. Keep the chosen package identity distinct from its executable name. Verify: Start from a clean controlled cache and record the resolved package/version; verify the MCP launch command selects that exact artifact. 2. Prefer a preinstalled tool built from a reviewed lockfile or verified artifact, with an approved registry and integrity data for dependencies. Audit additional --with packages and executable-search paths. Verify: Compare fresh installations in controlled environments and investigate any dependency/artifact digest differences. 3. Run the server with only task-required credentials and workspace permissions. Propose version updates through review, provenance checks and regression tests rather than enabling automatic latest resolution. Verify: Verify the launched process identity/environment and exercise a required tool after a reviewed update without expanding its permissions."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "agentMcpScan/v1": "6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f"
          },
          "properties": {
            "agentMcpRemediation": {
              "agent_mcp_relevance": "An MCP client often launches a package with its local user permissions and injected credentials. Unpinned npx/uvx resolution can replace the tool implementation between launches without a reviewed configuration change.",
              "applicability": [
                "Inspect the actual package runner, registry and cache/lock behavior; a project lockfile may not govern an independent ephemeral runner.",
                "An exact version reduces movement but does not prove package integrity or constrain all transitive dependencies."
              ],
              "catalog_sha256": "6ea5b70b817f35b68352ce9b7b443b1c01139ba7b94ee2631f5db5ef7521b96e",
              "catalog_version": "1.0.0",
