          "message": {
            "text": "A container base or deployment image uses a mutable reference rather than a content digest. The bytes can change between builds or deployments. Remediation: Pin approved image digests, track provenance and SBOMs, and update through reviewed vulnerability-remediation workflows. Agent/MCP relevance: Agent/MCP deployments may execute a different tool stack when a mutable image tag moves. That changes the code holding credentials and enforcing tool policy without a matching application source change. Fix steps: 1. Replace mutable base/deployment references with the approved registry image@sha256 digest, retaining a human-readable version where useful. Record the intended platform or multi-platform index. Verify: Resolve the approved reference through the build/deployment system and verify the running image digest matches the recorded artifact/platform. 2. Associate the digest with build provenance, an SBOM and a separate vulnerability scan; verify the publisher and build process before approving it. Verify: Trace the selected digest to the expected build and verify the SBOM and vulnerability results apply to that exact artifact. 3. Use automation to propose digest updates, rebuild and run agent/MCP regression and policy checks, then roll out the reviewed artifact. Verify: Exercise rollback to a previously approved digest and confirm updates do not silently widen runtime permissions."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "agentMcpScan/v1": "055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8"
          },
          "properties": {
            "agentMcpRemediation": {
              "agent_mcp_relevance": "Agent/MCP deployments may execute a different tool stack when a mutable image tag moves. That changes the code holding credentials and enforcing tool policy without a matching application source change.",
              "applicability": [
                "Inspect the image selected by the actual build/deployment and platform; tags may already be constrained by external admission policy.",
                "Digest pinning controls content identity, not whether the pinned content is safe or current."
              ],
              "catalog_sha256": "6ea5b70b817f35b68352ce9b7b443b1c01139ba7b94ee2631f5db5ef7521b96e",
              "catalog_version": "1.0.0",
              "control_ids": [
